import{_ as o,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-016 — Compact nav controls and one More menu","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-016-compact-nav-and-more-menu.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-016-compact-nav-and-more-menu.md"}'),s={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-016-compact-nav-and-more-menu.md"};function r(c,e,i,d,h,l){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="uxd-016-—-compact-nav-controls-and-one-more-menu" tabindex="-1">UXD-016 — Compact nav controls and one More menu <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-016-—-compact-nav-controls-and-one-more-menu" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-016 — Compact nav controls and one More menu&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-12 (proposed and decided)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator, 2026-11-12 — &quot;A6 — compact bar + More menu (High contrast, Share, Debug); nav height 52 px in one token; 32 px toggles on fine pointers, 44 on touch&quot; (&quot;A3–A6 answers&quot;, <code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code>); the hamburger break stays at 1219 px in A6 (&quot;A4–A6 open items&quot;, answer 5a, same file), lowered later after a 14-locale measurement (deferred list L2)</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: N1; slice A6; closes UXS-000 SC-1 (nav height) and the nav z-index mismatch</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/components/Nav.svelte</code>, <code>src/lib/components/LocalePicker.svelte</code> (trigger sizing and look), <code>src/lib/styles/tokens.css</code> (<code>--nav-bar-height</code>, <code>--nav-height</code>, <code>--nav-btn-fine</code>, <code>--nav-btn-touch</code>), the literal tops and <code>var(--nav-height, NNpx)</code> fallbacks that disagreed with the token; <a href="./../IA">IA §shell-regions</a>; Design System §4.1 / §5.1 (<code>docs/concept/05_Design_System.md</code>); AGENTS.md (Nav block); <code>docs/adr/TA.md</code> nav paragraph; <code>src/lib/components/README.md</code></li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The eight right-hand controls were 44 × 44 on every pointer (a <code>width: 32px</code> lost to <code>min-width: 44px</code>), 14 px apart: a 392 px cluster beside links about 27 px tall, in a 60 px bar that IA, AGENTS and the Design System called 52 px (<code>--nav-bar-height: 60px</code>, and <code>--nav-height</code> re-typed the literal <code>60px</code>, so editing the first did nothing). High contrast, Share and Debug sat in the primary chrome for every visitor.</p><h2 id="options" tabindex="-1">Options <a class="header-anchor" href="#options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Options&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A. A compact bar plus one More menu. B. High contrast, Debug and Share inside the Settings sheet. C. Compact sizing only, all controls kept. For the height: 52 px everywhere, 48 / 56 by pointer, or keep 60 px and fix the docs.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Option A. Bar, left to right: audio tour, locale, science lens, settings, More (the hamburger on its own breakpoints). The More button is a WAI-ARIA menu button; its panel holds High contrast and Debug overlays (<code>menuitemcheckbox</code>) and Share this view (<code>menuitem</code>). The panel renders outside the <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>, so the bar&#39;s roving arrows never reach its rows. The switch rows keep the menu open so the flip is visible; Share closes it. On phones (≤ 600 px) there is no More button: the same three actions are drawer rows, rendered from the same list.</p><p>Sizes: 32 × 32 on a fine primary pointer (<code>(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)</code>), 44 × 44 otherwise, both axes (<code>--nav-btn-fine</code>, <code>--nav-btn-touch</code>); gap 6 px fine, 4 px touch, 2 px on phones; the locale chip is 32 high with a 40 px minimum width. The look is the A4 chip&#39;s (<a href="./UXD-014-one-chip-and-filter">UXD-014</a>): outline at rest, soft accent fill + accent edge + white glyph when on, hover lifts a control at rest only, focus ring <code>--color-focus</code>; one <code>.nav-btn</code> base replaces the five copied rule blocks. The lens gold and the debug orange stay as semantic state colours.</p><p>Height: one 52 px bar from one token (<code>--nav-bar-height: 52px</code>; <code>--nav-height</code> is that plus the safe-area inset). The literal tops and fallbacks that disagreed follow the token. The nav is <code>z-index: 40</code>.</p><p>The hamburger break stays at 1219 px: the old measurement (ru 1210 px, 2026-11-04) was made with the 392 px cluster; the per-locale measurement in <code>tests/e2e/nav-controls.spec.ts</code> reports the new widths and the break is lowered in a later step the operator approves (L2).</p><p>Defaults taken without asking: the TV layout also shows the More button (the menu is arrow and OK operable and the old classes for the three controls are gone, so a second bar rendering would need them back); no new Umami events; Share behaviour unchanged (no &quot;link copied&quot; notice); no new locale key (the trigger reuses <code>layout_footer_more</code>, the rows reuse <code>nav_high_contrast_aria</code>, <code>nav_share</code>, <code>nav_debug_group_aria</code>).</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The cluster is about 192 px instead of 392 px on a fine pointer; contrast, share and debug are two clicks and have visible labels and states (a check mark and <code>aria-checked</code>, no English On / Off); every <code>--nav-height</code> consumer sits 8 px higher; the sticky launches month header, which already assumed 52 px, is now flush with the bar. The Share button, the Aa button and the debug toggle are gone from the bar, and with them <code>.contrast-toggle</code>, <code>.share-toggle</code> and the nav <code>.debug-toggle</code>; <code>mobile-layout</code>, <code>chip</code> and <code>pwa</code> specs changed with them. The More menu sits above the DebugPanel and the settings sheet (z 92 / 91 against 90), closes when the window crosses 600 px, and hides in exhibit mode.</p><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>A6-CHECK violations: 0</code> (the brief&#39;s check, <code>docs/wip/2026-11-12-slice-A6-brief.md</code> §11); <code>tests/e2e/nav-controls.spec.ts</code> (fine and coarse sizes and gaps, the one bar height, the menu keyboard flow, the unchanged roving toolbar, axe on the open menu, the phone drawer, the per-locale width report); the A4 sweep in <code>tests/e2e/chip.spec.ts</code> allow-lists the new classes. Not checked yet: the screenshots of the brief&#39;s section 9 and a run of the specs in a browser.</p>',16)])])}const m=o(s,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
